WEBVTT

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.310
My lady!

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.110
My humblest apologies.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.810
In temporarily opening our hotel to the public as an emergency shelter,

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:25.020
...we are causing you substantial inconvenience.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:29.050
I don't mind. Please do everything you can for them.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.060
It reminds me of fifteen or so years ago.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.920
Things were like this at the time of XX, too.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.510
Those people... Can't they be treated at a hospital?

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.580
Every hospital says they are full to capacity with the injured.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.850
We have taken care of first-aid treatment, but...

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.090
They'll be fine, right?

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.460
That I cannot say.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:46.830
In the old days, these sorts of injuries and burns were easily healed, you see, using cloning technology.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.600
Cloning?

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.380
Because it made skin grafts and organ transplants possible without any rejection responses.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.680
How was the cultivating done?

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.150
I've heard that they made use of pigs.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.590
After all, it most certainly wasn't appropriate to use women's bodies.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.080
Oink...

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:10.950
Kiyoko...

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.040
Who's there?

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.770
It's me, Keiko.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:43.500
Hey!

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.800
This is sudden. What's the matter?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:52.070
That's my line. I couldn't get in touch with you at all, so I thought maybe something had happened.

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:55.240
Sorry to make you worry. I'm fine.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.370
Are you sure?

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:00.150
If you're sick or not feeling well, how about I make you something?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.580
Like a "Keiko Special" bowl of rice and porridge?

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.210
Sorry, but I'm honestly all right.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.850
Hey, I came all the way here because I was worried...

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.360
Is somebody here? A guest?

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:17.320
No, nobody special.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.000
Oh, lucky you!

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.800
I'd like to take some unapproved time off for that too!

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.370
What? Don't go talking nonsense!

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.160
Lucky you!

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:32.870
Come on!

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.510
Well then, I'll catch you later.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:38.000
Right! Thanks.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.050
It was a co-worker.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.360
I'm going out for a bit.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.900
I won't mind if you clear out of here while I'm gone.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.490
This piano's come back to life.

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:44.720
It was playing in your mind.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:49.900
You could hear it?

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.340
Continue...

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.010
Do you always come here?

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:44.280
Since about a month ago.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:48.160
I felt so sorry for it somehow.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.590
I found the tuning fork here too.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.760
You love pianos, don't you?

00:10:56.700 --> 00:11:00.160
In this world, there's not a single thing that goes the way you want it to.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:04.340
But pianos are different.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.340
If you gently touch the keys, they'll play a gentle tone for you.

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.870
And right now, what kind of...

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.060
Does it hurt?

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:34.060
You shouldn't rub it.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:39.460
This is the place where we first met.

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:41.210
Yeah...

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:44.810
It's raining again, just like that time.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:51.180
After what happened to the Settlement, things are crumbling to dust everywhere you look.

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:56.650
Destroying the Turangalila was a necessary act.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:08.430
The Sheltering Sky is a cocoon for the purpose of giving birth to a new human race.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:11.660
If the cocoon is taken away, the pupa will die.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:16.030
You humans are in the process of being reborn.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:21.170
What will happen when we are reborn into a new human race?

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.310
Are you saying we can make a world that's a little less horrid than this one?

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.440
A world far more splendid than the world of now.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:32.190
By doing so, the Professor is attempting to purify the universe.

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:34.450
I've had enough of Dad's delusions.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:50.430
Human beings are stupid, so we've waged wars and polluted the Earth.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.770
But we've still managed to muddle our way through this far.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.620
So all this stuff about a new human race, a splendid world and whatnot,

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:59.140
...is just needless meddling, isn't it?!

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.990
To make your own two children into miserable wretches...

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:05.550
...and then talk about purifying the universe is beyond ridiculous.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:10.160
I'm positive what you call the "new human race" will be stupid too.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.590
It's something my dad is trying to do after all.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.530
It's bound to be a botched job.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:34.940
Don't rub your eye.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:02.400
I got it.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.090
How can you be so gentle?

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:18.790
Is it because I'm Enkidu's daughter?

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:20.130
No...

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.030
Really?

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:23.760
Really...

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:31.570
You asked me before what kind of sound the piano was making.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:34.310
Yeah...

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:43.010
Ever since I was a little girl, the piano had been my escape, because reality was just so horrible.

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:49.720
We took shelter from the rain under that piano, then we fled inside here and met you.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:58.960
Just maybe you might save me from this reality...

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:00.830
That's what I thought.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:07.280
At the time, that's really what I thought!

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:19.780
First it rained while the sun was shining, now we've got this sort of creepy sunset.

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:21.650
Yeah...

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:24.890
Hey, I'd like you to give me some Dynamis.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.260
Huh?

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:28.380
I don't feel good.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:31.360
Could you please?

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.130
It's a shame what it's doing to your beauty.

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:35.600
Hey, you've gotten the hang of this smooth talking thing.

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.850
Your big sister is all right.

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:56.910
Thank you!

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:05.800
Whoa, that's some serious malice!

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:07.200
It's not Gilgamesh!

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.130
Is this...

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:10.430
It's the Blattaria!

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:26.540
What's going on?

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:39.220
What on earth is this about?!

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:45.960
I apologize for the disturbance.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:49.040
I'm asking what this is about.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:51.410
A spy has been discovered.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:54.210
Or should I say, a friend to the terrorists.

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:57.080
What are you talking about?

00:18:57.080 --> 00:19:00.080
The major explosion at the Turangalila yesterday...

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:04.150
We are pursuing a person suspected of abetting that terrorist act.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.560
Show it to her.

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:07.990
Yes, Sir.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:29.880
We have been given a law enforcement task by the judiciary,

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:33.680
and have come to take a suspect, Tatsuya Madoka, into custody.

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:41.290
That data demonstrates that according to the investigation,

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:47.590
...the wave this suspect emitted inside the Turangalila led to Gilgamesh being allowed to gain entry.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:51.530
Doubtless this, too, is something fabricated by your company.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.500
The law is the law, you know.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:07.810
Stop it!

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:16.130
Madoka...

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:18.620
I would like to carry this out peaceably.

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:21.190
How do you feel about that?

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:52.750
I have a fine attorney. Don't worry.

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:03.300
All this for one child. Adults sure have it rough too, huh?

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.540
That's about right.

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:16.610
Damn!

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:20.460
Contact my attorney, please. Immediately.

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:21.820
As you wish, my lady.

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:24.220
<i>What was that about?</i>

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:26.760
<i>Who were those guys?</i>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.050
We keep running into each other today.

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:27.180
I'm here on a home visit.

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:28.790
A new member of Gilgamesh, is it?

00:23:28.790 --> 00:23:32.120
It would be no joke if I were to be tossed out onto the street stark naked, would it?

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:33.620
I'll show you something interesting.

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.350
What do you think this means?

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:37.730
This'll be a good lesson about the world.

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:40.130
Have you never attempted to join their group?

00:23:40.130 --> 00:23:41.930
So then, have you had contact with Enkidu?

00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:43.230
What is Enkidu's objective?

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:45.100
What is your relationship with Enkidu?

00:23:45.100 --> 00:23:48.370
We've taken a look at your entire body, from head to toe.

00:23:48.370 --> 00:23:50.530
This old man's quite jealous.

00:23:50.940 --> 00:23:53.600
It's wonderful to be young, isn't it?
